# Enum organization

## New domain enums

Place enums for a domain under `src/enum/<module>/`:

```
src/enum/pricing/
  fee-component-type.enum.ts
  connector-output-type.enum.ts
  index.ts
```

- One enum per file (`*.enum.ts`).
- Module folder name scopes the domain — drop redundant prefixes from file/export names when the folder already provides context (e.g. `ConnectorOutputType` in `pricing/`, not `PricingConnectorOutputType`).
- Add `src/enum/<module>/index.ts` re-exporting the module's enums.
- Re-export from root `src/enum/index.ts` so consumers keep using `import { X } from 'spotcharge-types'`.

## Legacy flat enums

Existing enums in `src/enum/*.enum.ts` stay until that domain is migrated. Do not move legacy enums into a new module folder unless you are actively migrating that domain.

## API models

Domain API models under `src/models/api/<module>/` should import enums from `../../../enum/<module>`, not from the flat enum root.
